      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يَطُوفُ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَ الْمَرْوَةِ أَ يَسْتَرِيحُ قَالَ نَعَمْ إِنْ شَاءَ جَلَسَ عَلَى الصَّفَا وَ الْمَرْوَةِ وَ بَيْنَهُمَا فَيَجْلِسُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al Halby who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the man who performs <span class=\"iTxt\">Tawaaf</span> between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa, can he rest?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes, if he so desires to sit upon Al-Safa and Al-Marwa, and between the two, so he can sit’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ibn abu ‘Umayr has narrated from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who performs Sa‘y between al-Safa’ and al-Marwah: if he can rest. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, he can do so on al-Safa’ or al-Marwah or in between.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
